/*
Tree DP rerooting.

Let dpDown[v] = number of valid colorings inside subtree of v
(when rooted at 1) such that v is black and all black vertices in that subtree
form one connected component containing v.

For a child u of v, inside u-subtree either:
- no black vertex exists there: all white -> 1 way
- black vertices exist and must connect through u, so u must be black:
  dpDown[u] ways
Thus contribution from child u is (1 + dpDown[u]).

So:
dpDown[v] = product over children u of (1 + dpDown[u]) mod M.

For answer ans[v], we need the same quantity considering all neighbors,
assuming v is black:
ans[v] = product over neighbors u of (1 + waysFromNeighborSide(u -> v))

For children, waysFromNeighborSide = dpDown[child].
For parent side, compute via rerooting.

Let up[v] = number of valid colorings of the component outside v-subtree
(on the parent side) such that if there are black vertices there, they form
a connected component containing parent of v and can connect to v through parent.
Then contribution from parent side to v is (1 + up[v])? Careful:

When v is black, for each adjacent side:
- choose no black vertices on that side: 1
- choose a connected black set touching the neighbor: number of ways from that side

For parent side of v, the "touching neighbor" is parent p, so side contribution is
1 + sideWays, where sideWays is number of colorings outside subtree(v) with p black
and black vertices connected through p. Define parVal[v] = sideWays.
Then:
ans[v] = product(children c)(1 + dpDown[c]) * (v==root ? 1 : (1 + parVal[v]))

To compute parVal[child]:
Suppose parent is v and child is c.
Outside c-subtree, with v black, each other adjacent side of v contributes:
- parent side of v: (v==root ? 1 : (1 + parVal[v]))
- every other child t != c: (1 + dpDown[t])
Their product is exactly the number of valid colorings on the "rest of tree"
where black vertices (if any) are connected and contain v.
Thus:
parVal[c] = product_of_all_contributions_around_v_excluding_c

We can compute efficiently with prefix/suffix products over neighbors in rooted order.
*/

public class Main {
    static class FastScanner {
        private final InputStream in;
        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1 << 16];
        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;

        FastScanner(InputStream is) {
            in = is;
        }

        private int read() throws IOException {
            if (ptr >= len) {
                len = in.read(buffer);
                ptr = 0;
                if (len <= 0) return -1;
            }
            return buffer[ptr++];
        }

        long nextLong() throws IOException {
            int c;
            do c = read(); while (c <= ' ' && c != -1);
            long sign = 1;
            if (c == '-') {
                sign = -1;
                c = read();
            }
            long val = 0;
            while (c > ' ') {
                val = val * 10 + (c - '0');
                c = read();
            }
            return val * sign;
        }

        int nextInt() throws IOException {
            return (int) nextLong();
        }
    }

    static int N;
    static long MOD;
    static ArrayList<Integer>[] g;
    static int[] parent;
    static int[] order;
    static long[] down;
    static long[] parVal;
    static long[] ans;

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner(System.in);
        N = fs.nextInt();
        MOD = fs.nextLong();

        g = new ArrayList[N + 1];
        for (int i = 1; i <= N; i++) g[i] = new ArrayList<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < N - 1; i++) {
            int x = fs.nextInt();
            int y = fs.nextInt();
            g[x].add(y);
            g[y].add(x);
        }

        parent = new int[N + 1];
        order = new int[N];
        buildRootedTreeIterative(1);

        down = new long[N + 1];
        parVal = new long[N + 1];
        ans = new long[N + 1];

        // bottom-up
        for (int i = N - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            int v = order[i];
            long prod = 1 % MOD;
            for (int to : g[v]) {
                if (to == parent[v]) continue;
                prod = (prod * ((1 + down[to]) % MOD)) % MOD;
            }
            down[v] = prod;
        }

        // top-down reroot
        parVal[1] = 0; // unused for root; contribution is just 1
        for (int idx = 0; idx < N; idx++) {
            int v = order[idx];

            int deg = g[v].size();
            long[] contrib = new long[deg];
            for (int i = 0; i < deg; i++) {
                int to = g[v].get(i);
                if (to == parent[v]) {
                    contrib[i] = (v == 1) ? 1 % MOD : (1 + parVal[v]) % MOD;
                } else {
                    contrib[i] = (1 + down[to]) % MOD;
                }
            }

            long[] pref = new long[deg + 1];
            long[] suff = new long[deg + 1];
            pref[0] = 1 % MOD;
            for (int i = 0; i < deg; i++) pref[i + 1] = (pref[i] * contrib[i]) % MOD;
            suff[deg] = 1 % MOD;
            for (int i = deg - 1; i >= 0; i--) suff[i] = (suff[i + 1] * contrib[i]) % MOD;

            ans[v] = pref[deg];

            for (int i = 0; i < deg; i++) {
                int to = g[v].get(i);
                if (to == parent[v]) continue;
                parVal[to] = (pref[i] * suff[i + 1]) % MOD;
            }
        }

        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 1; i <= N; i++) {
            sb.append(ans[i]).append('\n');
        }
        System.out.print(sb.toString());
    }

    static void buildRootedTreeIterative(int root) {
        int[] stack = new int[N];
        int top = 0;
        stack[top++] = root;
        parent[root] = 0;
        int idx = 0;

        while (top > 0) {
            int v = stack[--top];
            order[idx++] = v;
            for (int to : g[v]) {
                if (to == parent[v]) continue;
                parent[to] = v;
                stack[top++] = to;
            }
        }
    }
}

#include <stdio.h>
